# 00reaper Processes Guide

This guide describes the 00reaper processes that manage the 00OS development workflow.

## Core Workflow Processes

### Initialization and Context
- [reaper-init.md](mdc:00OS/processes/00reaper/reaper-init.md): Initialize 00reaper context and system understanding
- [reaper-read-files.md](mdc:00OS/processes/00reaper/reaper-read-files.md): Read files from specified directories
- [reaper-overwrite.md](mdc:00OS/processes/00reaper/reaper-overwrite.md): Generate context files from directory contents

### Development Workflow
- [reaper-os-commands-workflow.md](mdc:00OS/processes/00reaper/reaper-os-commands-workflow.md): Orchestrate the development workflow
- [reaper-analyze-tasks.md](mdc:00OS/processes/00reaper/reaper-analyze-tasks.md): Analyze and prioritize development tasks
- [reaper-implement.md](mdc:00OS/processes/00reaper/reaper-implement.md): Execute changes to 00OS processes

### Synchronization
- [reaper-sync.md](mdc:00OS/processes/00reaper/reaper-sync.md): Sync 00OS contents to Cursor rules
- [reaper-update.md](mdc:00OS/processes/00reaper/reaper-update.md): Update context with latest workflow info

## Development Guidelines

When working with 00reaper processes:

1. Start with `reaper-init` to establish context
2. Use `reaper-os-commands-workflow` to manage development cycles
3. Keep context up-to-date using `reaper-overwrite` and `reaper-update`
4. Sync changes to Cursor rules using `reaper-sync`

## Process Dependencies

The processes work together in a specific order:
1. Initialize → `reaper-init`
2. Read/Analyze → `reaper-read-files`, `reaper-analyze-tasks`
3. Implement → `reaper-implement`
4. Update → `reaper-update`, `reaper-overwrite`
5. Sync → `reaper-sync`

